pouch boundary-line patch 0069 - the kernel's note table, and calls a note can interrupt.

Operator votes 18, 19 and 20 (2026-11-03); ARCHITECTURE 8.8.3 and POUCH-DESIGN 6.4.

Pouch used to register its dispatcher from a constructor, for every program. To the
kernel that read as "caught" for every note, so a SIG_DFL SIGINT or SIGTERM armed no
terminate latch: a program blocked in a wait did not die until the wait ended, and ^Z did
nothing. Nothing unwound a wait for a real handler either.

  src/signal/_pouch_signal.c    The constructor registers nothing; it keeps the SIGPIPE
      default mask. A program with no handler has none, and the kernel takes every note's
      default itself, in a wait as well as at the tail.
  src/signal/sigaction.c        Every disposition writes the note's row through
      SYS_note_dispose. A real handler registers the dispatcher first, so until its row
      lands every note reaches the dispatcher, which reads the table. SIG_DFL with no row
      ever written writes nothing. A refused row puts the old table entry back and answers
      the errno. The comment saying SA_RESTART needed nothing was false: musl re-issues no
      call, and the row's flag is what restarts one, in the kernel.
  src/unistd/pause.c            pause() sits on SYS_poll over no fds. SYS_ppoll is an
      ENOSYS sentinel, so pause returned at once.
  src/select/poll.c, select.c   A poll or select over no fds sleeps for the timeout
      instead of answering ENOSYS; the kernel has that sleep now.
  src/process/_pouch_process.c  waitpid surfaces EINTR. Every failure read as ECHILD.
  src/network/_pouch_socket.c, accept.c, connect.c  The listen open and the data open set
      SYS_WALK_OPEN_OINTR and answer EINTR. SYS_srv_accept answers EINTR. A connect that
      a note unwound leaves the slot in the new POUCH_SOCK_CONNECTING: the request stands
      (POSIX), so a retry waits on the data open and never dials again, and I/O on such a
      slot waits for the connection first, which is what poll-then-use after an interrupted
      connect needs. pouch_net_open_conn_file now reports the open's errno.
  arch/aarch64/bits/syscall.h.in  __NR_note_dispose 139. After a musl re-vendor, extend
      0001's awk filter: m["note_dispose"]="139";

Witnesses: pouch-hello-signals `dfl`, `dfl-reset`, `dfl-after-handler`, `exec-dfl`,
`intr-norestart`, `intr-restart`, `signal-restart`, `quiet`, `pause`, `nanosleep`,
`wait-norestart`, `wait-restart`, `fork-read`, `empty-poll`; pouch-hello-sockets `accept`
and `recv`; pouch-hello-net `accept-eintr`, `accept-restart`, `connect`.

